<FieldGuideLayout
  title="UI container .lzs files — text audit"
  description="Step-305 confirmed the 16 player-facing UI container files plus the inputstr/ directory carry zero translatable text. They are TAD/RESC graphics archives (sprites, palettes, cells) and internal kana-keyboard data. The text these UIs display comes from the message-system msg*.ofs files, not from the containers themselves."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'File Formats', href: `${base}/field-guide/file-formats/` },
    { label: 'UI containers (text audit)' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Sixteen <code>.lzs</code> files under <code>data/</code> sit behind the
    most text-heavy UI surfaces in the game: the bulletin board, mail editor,
    item-name entry, locker, mail-order list, sale ranking, music-select
    screen, shop info / profile / "make profile", default-costume picker,
    catch-display, and the lower-screen letter and BBS chrome. The
    <code>inputstr/</code> directory adds five more files behind the
    on-screen Japanese kana keyboard. The step-305 audit (2026-05-20) put
    every one of them through a strict UTF-16-LE kana-required scan to
    settle whether any of them carry translatable text the toolchain had
    missed.
  </p>

  <h2>Headline result</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>19 of the 21 audited files are pure binary game-data
    containers</strong> (TAD/RESC graphics, palette, screen, and cell
    archives) with zero player-visible Japanese text. The two text-bearing
    files are inside <code>inputstr/</code> and are part of the on-screen
    keyboard / profanity-filter machinery — translating them would break
    Japanese name input, not enable English UI. <strong>No new translation
    work is opened by this audit.</strong>
  </p>

